Cap the free kernel VA the kmem ranges are divided from

The ranges are sized from every free byte of kernel VA, tens of terabytes here, and
with 4 KiB pages each 128 KiB of range wants a kmem_page_meta entry.  The metadata
claim cannot cover that, so kmem_get_new_chunk() runs out of meta and returns NULL
forever, which is the spin at kmem_locate_space.  Cap the free VA at 128 GiB.
---
diff --git a/osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c b/osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c
index 2927d4b..3afcc4b 100644
--- a/osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c
+++ b/osfmk/vm/vm_kern.c
@@ -3494,6 +3494,16 @@ kmem_add_extra_claims(void)
 	}
 	assert((total_claims & PAGE_MASK) == 0);
 	largest_free_size -= total_claims;
+	/*
+	 * nio: this is every free byte of kernel VA, tens of terabytes, and the
+	 * three ranges derived from it then need far more kmem_page_meta entries
+	 * than the metadata claim can hold, so the first chunk request runs out
+	 * of meta and spins.  A hundred and twenty-eight gigabytes of free VA is
+	 * more than this board can ever use.
+	 */
+	if (largest_free_size > (vm_map_size_t)128 * 1024 * 1024 * 1024) {
+		largest_free_size = (vm_map_size_t)128 * 1024 * 1024 * 1024;
+	}
 
